Author: Carson M / pyke.io and Earshot contributors
License option used by Lince: MIT, reproduced in LICENSE-MIT.txt

Lince uses the embedded default predictor through Earshot's Rust API to detect
voice in mono 16 kHz input. No external inference runtime or model download is
required. This detects speech activity; it does not decide whether a request
addresses Fiote or choose a recipient.
